In general, the annual growth rate for the Hinterland regions has shown a steady increase for
the three Census periods. The largest occurred between 1991 and 2002 as indicated in Figure 8 in
absolute term. Figure 9 also compares the annual growth rates between the two geographic zones.
This figure shows the fluctuating growth rates of the Coastland population. There was a decrease
